## Transport rule

Prefer CLI invocations over MCP transports for driving another agent
harness: `opencode run` or `codex exec` rather than an MCP
tool call into the same harness. MCP transports to agent harnesses have
been observed hanging past their expected completion time, and returning
empty results from a server that finished its work correctly on the
CLI side. Use CLI invocations as the default; treat an MCP path to another
harness as a fallback that needs its own pre-vet echo test before a wave
depends on it.

## Reviewer pre-vet

Before a wave or gate depends on any reviewer named above, run the pre-vet
checklist in `MODEL-CLASSES.md`: reachability, usage headroom, permission
profile, and model identity. An unvetted, quota-exhausted, or
under-permissioned reviewer defers per `PROCESS.md`.

